(88, 3, 'California remains world’s No. 4 economy - barely', 'Just $250 billion of business output – a 6% gap – separates California and Japan, Great Britain and India for the No. 4 spot.', 'California’s economy remains No. 4 on the global stage – barely!\nMy trusty spreadsheet once again looked into a vanity scorecard that compares the state’s gross domestic product, a broad measure of business output, with the International Monetary Fun... [1048 chars]', 'The Mercury News', 'https://www.mercurynews.com/2026/07/18/california-remains-worlds-no-4-economy-barely/', 'https://www.mercurynews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/The-worlds-No.-4-economy-by-GDP-estimates-from-US-BEA-and-IMF@2x-1.jpeg?w=1024&h=576', 'supply-chain', 'neutral', 0, 0, 0.0000, '2026-07-18 15:08:34', '2026-07-19 13:37:10', '2026-07-19 13:37:10'),
