(142, 10, '‘Gateway to Asean’: South Korea bets on Vietnam hub for food expansion', 'Vietnam will be positioned as a logistics and distribution base aimed at growing demand for South Korean food products across the region.', 'As Southeast Asia emerges as one of South Korea’s most important trading regions, Seoul is positioning Vietnam as a logistics and distribution base for a wider push to turn the popularity of Korean culture into sustained demand for Korean food across... [1044 chars]', 'South China Morning Post', 'https://www.scmp.com/week-asia/economics/article/3360840/gateway-asean-south-korea-bets-vietnam-hub-food-expansion', 'https://cdn.i-scmp.com/sites/default/files/styles/og_image_scmp_generic/public/d8/images/canvas/2026/07/16/9d4ce0e7-71f1-41e9-893c-40cbf6055f7b_c5c4a174.jpg?itok=aGHGP-Gy&v=1784212941', 'supply-chain', 'positive', 4, 0, 1.0000, '2026-07-17 03:00:07', '2026-07-20 05:30:56', '2026-07-20 05:30:56'),
(143, 10, 'Fact Check: Viral blaze is from South Korea, NOT Iran\'s attacks on Gulf countries', 'A viral video was shared as footage of Iran\'s attacks on US bases in the Gulf. India Today Fact Check found it actually showed a logistics centre fire in South Korea from November 2025.', 'After a brief ceasefire, tensions have once again escalated in West Asia, with Iran launching attacks on US military infrastructure in the Gulf in response to American strikes on Iranian targets.\nAmid the rising tension, a video has gone viral on soc... [1531 chars]', 'India Today', 'https://www.indiatoday.in/fact-check/story/south-korea-fire-video-fact-check-viral-clip-falsely-linked-to-iran-attacks-in-gulf-2949476-2026-07-16', 'https://akm-img-a-in.tosshub.com/indiatoday/images/story/202607/fact-check-164940123-16x9_0.jpg?VersionId=mEdy5GwfS8tvRwwDIOh2LEnbTFXZj4Cx', 'supply-chain', 'negative', 2, 16, -0.8235, '2026-07-16 15:52:25', '2026-07-20 05:30:56', '2026-07-20 05:30:56'),
(144, 10, 'South Korea Triples Deposit Margin For Leveraged ETFs', 'Seoul is tripling the cash needed to trade leveraged Samsung and SK Hynix ETFs after 24 emergency trading halts in nine weeks.', 'Seoul is tripling the cash Korean investors must hold to trade leveraged single-stock funds, an emergency attempt to contain the violent volatility that have triggered several emergency trading halts on the KOSPI index in recent weeks.\nSouth Korean e... [2319 chars]', 'Benzinga', 'https://www.benzinga.com/etfs/emerging-market-etfs/26/07/60495698/south-korea-leveraged-etfs-sk-hynix-samsung-single-stock-deposit-margin-volatility', 'https://cdn.benzinga.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=800,fit=crop/files/images/story/2026/07/16/National-Flag-Of-South-Korea-On-Satin--D.jpg', 'supply-chain', 'negative', 0, 10, -1.0000, '2026-07-16 13:25:39', '2026-07-20 05:30:56', '2026-07-20 05:30:56'),
(145, 10, 'South Korea and US: Navigating the Trade-Security Nexus', 'South Korea\'s National Security Council held a meeting with economic and diplomatic officials to discuss trade and security issues with the US. National Security Adviser Wi Sung-lac emphasized the importance of inter-departmental cooperation amidst rising external uncertainties. The meeting followed the return of South Korea\'s ambassador from the US.', 'South Korea\'s National Security Council held a significant meeting on Thursday, engaging economic and diplomatic officials to address crucial trade and security topics with the United States, as confirmed by the presidential office.\nNational Security... [636 chars]', 'Devdiscourse', 'https://www.devdiscourse.com/article/politics/3951145-south-korea-and-us-navigating-the-trade-security-nexus', 'https://www.devdiscourse.com/img?imageUrl=https://devdiscourse.blob.core.windows.net/aiimagegallery/12_05_2026_19_39_24_9634094.png&width=920&format=jpeg', 'supply-chain', 'positive', 3, 0, 1.0000, '2026-07-16 07:36:16', '2026-07-20 05:30:56', '2026-07-20 05:30:56'),
(146, 10, 'BOK hikes rates for first time in 3-1/2 years, signals more', 'South Korea\'s central bank raised its benchmark interest rate for the first ‌time in three-and-a-half years on Thursday and flagged more to come, as brisk growth in Asia\'s fourth-largest economy fanned inflation risks.', 'SEOUL, July 16 (Reuters) - South Korea\'s central bank raised its benchmark interest rate for the first ‌time in three-and-a-half years on Thursday and flagged more to come, as brisk growth in Asia\'s fourth-largest economy fanned inflation risks.\nSign... [1847 chars]', 'Reuters', 'https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/bok-hikes-rates-first-time-3-12-years-combat-inflation-won-slump-2026-07-16/', 'https://www.reuters.com/resizer/v2/AGMZLFJ22JOWTKCID5OVLKOVQI.jpg?auth=8b14599a0f34227e35ca2c054c8e9145f2365b1d5a4bf20f79381b2600017551&height=1005&width=1920&quality=80&smart=true', 'supply-chain', 'negative', 4, 7, -0.2727, '2026-07-16 01:07:02', '2026-07-20 05:30:56', '2026-07-20 05:30:56'),
(147, 4, 'US renews airstrikes on Iran, targets military assets used against commercial vessels', 'CENTCOM said it launched a fresh wave of air strikes against Iran for the ninth consecutive night. The United States said the operation is meant to weaken assets linked to attacks on shipping in the Strait of Hormuz.', 'The US Central Command (CENTCOM) said it has launched a fresh wave of airstrikes against Iran, continuing its military campaign targeting Iranian capabilities amid escalating tensions between Washington and Tehran.\nAccording to CENTCOM, the latest st... [2238 chars]', 'India Today', 'https://www.indiatoday.in/world/story/centcom-iran-air-strikes-ninth-night-strait-of-hormuz-shipping-threats-2951636-2026-07-20', 'https://akm-img-a-in.tosshub.com/indiatoday/images/story/202607/us-iran-war--hormuz--strait-of-hormuz-200734440-16x9_0.jpg?VersionId=yd0uAJO7DU2GZ0yBxKSwsO_wgUlRNosv', 'supply-chain', 'negative', 0, 8, -1.0000, '2026-07-20 00:09:17', '2026-07-20 05:31:02', '2026-07-20 05:31:02'),
(148, 4, 'US strikes Iran over troop deaths as Israel warns Tehran\'s attacks are coming close', 'The United States has launched more airstrikes at Iran, targeting the Revolutionary Guard in response to the killing of U.S. troops. Iran retaliated by firing missiles toward Jordan, risking a wider conflict with neighboring Israel. On Sunday, Kuwait, Jordan and Bahrain activated defenses against Iranian drones and missiles. Iran claims a nuclear site under construction was hit. The U.S. and Iran have returned closer to all-out war as last month’s interim deal meant to permanently end the fighting has crumbled and shipping traffic in the Strait of Hormuz has stalled. Both sides have targeted civilian infrastructure relied on by millions of people.', 'DUBAI, United Arab Emirates (AP) — The United States launched more airstrikes at Iran on Sunday in response to the killing of U.S. troops, and Iran fired missiles toward Jordan that risked widening the conflict into neighboring Israel.\nStep by step, ... [625 chars]', 'The Atlanta Journal-Constitution', 'https://www.ajc.com/news/2026/07/us-strikes-iran-over-troop-deaths-as-israel-warns-tehrans-attacks-are-coming-close/', 'https://images.ajc.com/resizer/v2/NM62YYP7AVFHNL7TX6YKC4GXRQ.jpg?auth=ebd6489d66d4bf3d6ef7d368ebbb548a902fe3bf3eaf1b758b23609f02ac442d&width=1200&height=630&smart=true', 'supply-chain', 'negative', 0, 14, -1.0000, '2026-07-19 15:02:30', '2026-07-20 05:31:02', '2026-07-20 05:31:02'),
(149, 4, 'Since 2006, a big South American lizard released by pet owners has been breeding across Florida: It raids the nests of native birds and even alligators to eat their eggs.', 'Science News: The Argentine black-and-white tegu was introduced to the United States through the exotic pet trade, but over the past two decades it has established .', 'The two prominent loreal scales between the eye and nostril, alongside its round pupils, identify it as belonging to the genus Salvator | Wikimedia Commons\nThe Argentine black-and-white tegu was introduced to the United States through the exotic pet ... [4389 chars]', 'Times of India', 'https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/since-2006-a-big-south-american-lizard-released-by-pet-owners-has-been-breeding-across-florida-it-raids-the-nests-of-native-birds-and-even-alligators-to-eat-their-eggs-/articleshow/132478643.cms', 'https://static.toiimg.com/thumb/msid-132479193,width-1280,height-720,resizemode-6,overlay-toi_sw,pt-32,y_pad-600/photo.jpg', 'supply-chain', 'neutral', 0, 0, 0.0000, '2026-07-19 07:40:00', '2026-07-20 05:31:02', '2026-07-20 05:31:02'),
(150, 4, 'US targets civilian infrastructure as they trade attacks with Iran', 'THE United States military said on Sunday that it carried out fresh attacks on Iran to “swiftly punish” Tehran for a devastating attack that killed two US military personnel.An area near Sirik in Iran’s Hormozgan province and Qeshm Island were hit on the eighth consecutive night of US air strikes on Iran, according to Iran’s Mehr and Tasnim news agencies.The news reports said there were no casualties and that residential and commercial infrastructure was not damaged in the attacks.', 'THE United States military said on Sunday that it carried out fresh attacks on Iran to “swiftly punish” Tehran for a devastating attack that killed two US military personnel.\nAn area near Sirik in Iran’s Hormozgan province and Qeshm Island were hit o... [2260 chars]', 'The Morning Star', 'https://morningstaronline.co.uk/article/us-targets-civilian-infrastructure-they-trade-attacks-iran', 'https://morningstaronline.co.uk/sites/default/files/styles/wide/public/2026-07/AP26200459872658.jpg.webp?itok=f_3V4X8c', 'supply-chain', 'negative', 0, 23, -1.0000, '2026-07-19 00:00:00', '2026-07-20 05:31:02', '2026-07-20 05:31:02'),
(151, 4, 'Iran, U.S. trade heavy fire; Israel continues to bomb Lebanon', 'The United States and Iran ramped up attacks on Saturday, while Israel and Lebanon did the same, as the Strait of Hormuz is still shut down.', 'July 18 (UPI) -- The United States and Iran ramped up attacks on Saturday, while Israel and Lebanon did the same, as the Strait of Hormuz is still shut down.\nThe U.S. Central Command said in a statement on X that it targeted \"surveillance sites, mili... [2837 chars]', 'UPI News', 'https://www.upi.com/Top_News/US/2026/07/18/iran-heavy-fire-israel-lebanon/6531784389575/', 'https://cdnph.upi.com/sv/ph/og/upi_com/6531784389575/2026/1/2de5c15fce85d992902c7604d0f4a3b7/v1.5/Iran-US-trade-heavy-fire-Israel-continues-to-bomb-Lebanon.jpg', 'supply-chain', 'negative', 0, 6, -1.0000, '2026-07-18 15:56:41', '2026-07-20 05:31:02', '2026-07-20 05:31:02'),
(152, 4, 'US Launches Safeguard Probe Into Imported Lamb Meat', 'The United States notified the World Trade Organization (WTO) Committee on Safeguards on 17 July that the investigation officially began on 13 July 2026.', 'The United States has started a safeguard investigation into imported lamb meat, opening a formal review to determine whether rising imports are harming or threatening the country\'s domestic lamb industry.\nThe United States notified the World Trade O... [2172 chars]', 'Devdiscourse', 'https://www.devdiscourse.com/article/business/3952333-us-launches-safeguard-probe-into-imported-lamb-meat', 'https://www.devdiscourse.com/img?imageUrl=https://devdiscourse.blob.core.windows.net/devnews/18_07_2026_14_51_55_341983.jpg&width=920&format=jpeg', 'supply-chain', 'positive', 2, 0, 1.0000, '2026-07-18 15:24:13', '2026-07-20 05:31:02', '2026-07-20 05:31:02'),
(153, 4, 'U.S., Iran trade fire for seventh consecutive day', 'The United States and Iran exchanged strikes aimed at infrastructure and military targets on Saturday as an Iranian negotiator said Tehran had suspended its commitments under the interim deal with the U.S. — snapping another fragile thread as the war shows no end in sight', 'The United States and Iran exchanged strikes aimed at infrastructure and military targets on Saturday as an Iranian negotiator said Tehran had suspended its commitments under the interim deal with the U.S. — snapping another fragile thread as the war... [1064 chars]', 'Africanews', 'https://www.africanews.com/2026/07/18/us-iran-trade-fire-for-seventh-consecutive-day/', 'https://images.euronews.com/articles/stories/09/84/26/72/1024x538_cmsv2_9d81acfa-716b-5da6-aeff-20af8ba5632e-9842672.jpg', 'supply-chain', 'negative', 0, 11, -1.0000, '2026-07-18 13:39:21', '2026-07-20 05:31:02', '2026-07-20 05:31:02'),
(154, 4, 'US and Iran trade strikes over Strait of Hormuz. Kuwait suffers infrastructure damage', 'The United States and Iran have exchanged strikes aimed at infrastructure and military targets as their battle over the Strait of Hormuz intensifies. The region has endured days of back-and-forth attacks in a conflict increasingly focused on control of the strait. The U.S. Central Command said early Saturday it had hit “surveillance sites, military logistics infrastructure, underground weapons storage, and maritime capabilities,” and Iran retaliated, with reports of strikes from Kuwait, Jordan and Iraq while air sirens also sounded multiple times in Bahrain. Iranian officials say recent U.S. strikes have killed dozens of people and wounded hundreds.', 'DUBAI, United Arab Emirates (AP) — The United States and Iran exchanged strikes aimed at infrastructure and military targets on Saturday as their battle over the Strait of Hormuz intensified.\nThe region has endured days of back-and-forth attacks in a... [476 chars]', 'The Atlanta Journal-Constitution', 'https://www.ajc.com/news/2026/07/us-and-iran-trade-strikes-over-strait-of-hormuz-kuwait-suffers-infrastructure-damage/', 'https://images.ajc.com/resizer/v2/EXRPN3BNOFGWROFKXF2I77LCSI.jpg?auth=f6eecd2d86a734cd5bf51cb3fabdd94a5c8e886c0f990b2e9912c0cd1f3a98b4&width=1200&height=630&smart=true', 'supply-chain', 'negative', 0, 23, -1.0000, '2026-07-18 13:01:54', '2026-07-20 05:31:02', '2026-07-20 05:31:02'),
(155, 4, 'FIFA World Cup Fever May Have Cost the US Economy $11.7 Bn in Lost Productivity', 'The FIFA World Cup may have delivered memorable moments for football fans, but it also came with a significant economic cost for the United States (US), according to a report by NDTV Profit.', 'The FIFA World Cup may have delivered memorable moments for football fans, but it also came with a significant economic cost for the United States (US), according to a report by NDTV Profit.\nCiting estimates from human resources software company UKG,... [1867 chars]', 'Outlook Business', 'https://www.outlookbusiness.com/news/fifa-world-cup-fever-may-have-cost-the-us-economy-117-bn-in-lost-productivity', 'https://media.assettype.com/outlookbusiness/2026-07-18/kfdaojf2/FIFA.jpg?w=1200&ar=40%3A21&auto=format%2Ccompress&ogImage=true&mode=crop&enlarge=true&overlay=false&overlay_position=bottom&overlay_width=100', 'supply-chain', 'positive', 6, 2, 0.4667, '2026-07-18 12:16:41', '2026-07-20 05:31:02', '2026-07-20 05:31:02'),
(156, 4, 'US-Iran strikes widen as Strait of Hormuz battle hits Kuwait infrastructure', 'The United States and Iran traded fresh strikes on military and infrastructure targets as fighting around the Strait of Hormuz escalated. The attacks hit vital facilities in Kuwait and Iran, underscoring the regional risks and growing pressure on shipping and energy supplies.', 'The United States and Iran exchanged fresh strikes on Saturday, with attacks targeting infrastructure and military sites as fighting over the Strait of Hormuz intensified. The latest round came after days of back-and-forth attacks in a conflict that ... [4300 chars]', 'India Today', 'https://www.indiatoday.in/world/story/strait-of-hormuz-conflict-us-iran-strikes-hit-kuwait-oil-desalination-facilities-ptag-2950826-2026-07-18', 'https://akm-img-a-in.tosshub.com/indiatoday/images/story/202607/pti-international-3-original_178-sixteen_nine.png?VersionId=up8U.ojE.ZZdVCLaALEgnpIo7TaYAWx9', 'supply-chain', 'negative', 0, 21, -1.0000, '2026-07-18 12:04:27', '2026-07-20 05:31:02', '2026-07-20 05:31:02'),
(157, 7, 'Pre-market action: Here\'s the trade setup for today\'s session', 'Domestic equities ended the week on a strong note, with Nifty rising. Analysts expect a gradual uptrend next week, driven by strong Q1 earnings. Investor focus will remain on management commentary and earnings reactions. India VIX fell, indicating reduced market fear. Foreign investors were net buyers of shares on Friday.', 'Domestic equities ended the week on a strong note, with Nifty rising 1.1% to close at 24,334 on Friday, driven by strong June-quarter earnings from index heavyweights across the IT and Financials sectors. Analysts say Indian equities are expected to ... [3140 chars]', 'The Economic Times', 'https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/pre-market-action-heres-the-trade-setup-for-todays-session/articleshow/132497342.cms', 'https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-132497331,width-1200,height-630,imgsize-122110,overlay-etmarkets/articleshow.jpg', 'supply-chain', 'positive', 11, 2, 0.7600, '2026-07-20 00:41:00', '2026-07-20 05:47:48', '2026-07-20 05:47:48'),
(158, 10, 'Iran Escalation; Japan Markets Closed', 'Asia-Pacific equities turned mixed as US-Iran escalation drove investor caution across the region. Australia\'s ASX 200 gained 0.10%, while South Korea\'s KOSPI declined 1.26% upon returning from a three-day weekend. Japan\'s Nikkei 225 was absent from trade due to a public holiday, leaving regional sentiment shaped primarily by the evolving geopolitical developments.', 'Asia-Pacific equity markets traded in mixed territory as investors reacted to the latest US-Iran escalation, shifting the primary driver of regional sentiment from a tech-led sell-off to geopolitical concerns. Japan\'s markets remained closed for a pu... [6605 chars]', 'scanx.trade', 'https://scanx.trade/stock-market-news/global/asia-pacific-markets-start-mixed-with-u-s-futures-flat-amid-geopolitical-risks-and-fed-focus/45023779', 'http://news-images.dhan.co/asia-pacific-markets-start-mixed-with-u-s-futures-flat-amid-geopolitical-risks-and-fed-focus.jpg', 'supply-chain', 'negative', 2, 5, -0.5000, '2026-07-20 00:51:00', '2026-07-20 05:57:57', '2026-07-20 06:02:10'),
(159, 7, 'India once dominated the textile trade. It needs institutions to make a mark again', 'India today possesses a fully integrated textile value chain, from cotton to spinning, weaving, processing, garment manufacturing and exports. The key catch is the employment intensity of the sector', 'Advertisement\nIndependent India’s textile journey has been an effort to reverse this. India today possesses a fully integrated textile value chain, from cotton to spinning, weaving, processing, garment manufacturing and exports. The key catch is the ... [5089 chars]', 'The Indian Express', 'https://indianexpress.com/article/opinion/columns/india-once-dominated-the-textile-trade-it-needs-institutions-to-make-a-mark-again-10794122/', 'https://images.indianexpress.com/2026/07/textile-companies_20260311222200_20260407213018_20260513233037_20260719190524.jpg', 'supply-chain', 'neutral', 0, 0, 0.0000, '2026-07-20 00:50:07', '2026-07-20 05:58:11', '2026-07-20 05:58:11');
